<article class="env-lemma" id="0D4V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D4V">Lemma <span data-tag="0D4V">99.14.13</span>.</a> The stack in groupoids $\mathcal{P}\! \mathit{olarized}$ satisfies openness of versality over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathbf{Z})$. Similarly, after base change (Remark <a href="/tag/0D1N" data-tag="0D1N">99.14.5</a>) openness of versality holds over any Noetherian base scheme $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Artin's Axioms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CXU" data-tag="0CXU">98.20.3</a> and Lemmas <a href="/tag/0D42" data-tag="0D42">99.14.7</a>, <a href="/tag/0D44" data-tag="0D44">99.14.9</a>, <a href="/tag/0D43" data-tag="0D43">99.14.8</a>, and <a href="/tag/0D4T" data-tag="0D4T">99.14.11</a>. For the “usual” proof of this fact, please see the discussion in the remark following this proof. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>